(umount2(2) requires CAP_SYS_ADMIN/root, so this is NOT auto-run in CI -)
(deliberately no .expected file, so test.sh skips it.)
(Run manually with: sudo ./target/release/vox tests/manual_unmount.vox --run)
(or without root: unshare -rm ./target/release/vox tests/manual_unmount.vox --run)

Remove the directory called "/tmp/vox_test_unmount".
Create a directory called "/tmp/vox_test_unmount".
On error print "mkdir failed", exit 1.

Mount "tmpfs" at "/tmp/vox_test_unmount" with type "tmpfs".
On error print "tmpfs mount failed - are you root?", exit 1.

(Prove the mount is live: create a file inside it)
Open a file for writing called "marker" at "/tmp/vox_test_unmount/marker.txt".
Write "on the mount\n" to marker.
Close marker.

If "/tmp/vox_test_unmount/marker.txt" is available then,
    print "marker visible while mounted".

Unmount "/tmp/vox_test_unmount".
On error print "unmount failed", exit 1.

(After unmount the marker must be gone - it lived on the tmpfs)
If "/tmp/vox_test_unmount/marker.txt" is available then,
    print "FAIL: marker still visible after unmount",
    exit 1.
Print "marker gone after unmount - unmount verified".

(Lazy variant: mount again and detach)
Mount "tmpfs" at "/tmp/vox_test_unmount" with type "tmpfs".
On error print "second tmpfs mount failed", exit 1.
Unmount "/tmp/vox_test_unmount" lazily.
On error print "lazy unmount failed", exit 1.
Print "lazy unmount succeeded".

Remove the directory called "/tmp/vox_test_unmount".
On error print "rmdir failed", exit 1.
Print "cleanup complete".
